{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he lay with Bilhah his father's concubine.</b> Some explain, according to what the Sages said, that he removed his father's bed — he uprooted the bed from its place; the meaning of וישכב is like ובכל תבואתי תשרש."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The note interprets וישכב ('and he lay/slept') via the midrashic reading that Reuben moved Bilhah's bed, drawing on the root שכב in the sense of 'removing' as in the parallel root שרש ('to uproot') cited from ובכל תבואתי תשרש (Deut. 29:27)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:29.891381427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}